  "title": "Move Beyond Group-Based Assumptions",
  "description": "Move beyond group-based assumptions. Here’s how: - Gather facts: Get to know the person instead of relying on stereotypes. - Question your bias: Ask, “Am I assuming this because of a group association?” - Focus on individuality: Treat each person as unique, with their own qualities. Example: Instead of assuming a coworker isn’t good at public speaking because of their quiet nature, ask if they’ve had experience with it.",
